From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:26:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Linux host: a host log and structured crash reports under XDG
 state (#23)

horizon_run.py now keeps host-<title>-<time>-<pid>.log and writes
crash-<title>-<time>-<pid>.json under $XDG_STATE_HOME/nx2linux/logs, the
folder the Qt front end already uses. A report is made for a guest thread
fault, a boot fault, svcBreak and any uncaught Python exception, with the
fault, the call chain as module+offset, each thread's last 16 kernel calls
and the run's counters. A process that dies of a signal leaves a faulthandler
dump that the next run turns into a report. Reports hold no home path, user
name, key or package name, no game memory, no registers and no function name
of the game unless asked for. docs/linux/logs-and-crashes.md describes it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: The Linux host had no log file and no crash report: add them under XDG state, with no personal path or game data
Issue: Sunshine-Off/NX2Linux#23

